    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"Magnetotelluric (MT) and Audiomagnetotelluric (AMT) data were collected in Alaska by USGS during 1986-1992 as part of the Trans Alaskan Crustal Transect (TACT).  This transect follows the Alyeska pipeline corridor.  Other Alaskan MT data were collected for the US Department of Energy in 1985 by Dal Stanley of USGS.  Additional AMT data were collected in 1985-1987 by Carl Long of USGS in the Baird Mountains, Ambler River, and Livengood quadrangles as part of the Alaska Mineral Resources Assessment Program (AMRAP). In all, MT data were taken at 318 locations and AMT data were taken at 236 locations.  AMT work investigates electrical conductivity to depths of a few km, whereas MT investigates to tens of km. \r\n\r\nThe Alaskan MT and AMT data were collected and processed using computer systems that are now obsolete.  This CD-ROM was made to preserve these at-risk data for future use.  In many cases we were able to scan data sheets from the original surveys.  In other cases, we recovered what we could from the original computers and storage media.  We were able to retrieve much raw field data and interpreted AMT data in this way, but we found relatively few inverted resistivity models (interpretations) of the MT data.  Interpreted data, however, are probably what non-specialist users need most.  As time allowed, therefore, we made preliminary 1-D (re)interpretations of much of the MT data.  This CD-ROM contains such reinterpretations for 142 MT sites, 2 per site.  These 1-D interpretations can be improved by using data from nearby soundings and other constraints.\r\n\r\nMT data were taken by Dal Stanley at 43 sites (labeled \"A??WDS\") in 4 quadrangles.  Because these data were well interpreted and have been published, they are not considered to be at risk.  Therefore, although their locations are shown on the index maps, no data folders are provided for them. \r\n\r\nData on this CD are organized by 1:250,000-scale sheet (quadrangle).  MT and/or AMT data were collected in 23 quadrangles. You can bring up a map showing the locations of these 23 quadrangles by clicking \"Alaska 3-Degree Quad Locations\" or \"To Quad Map\" from any of several menus on the CD-ROM.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
